def add(title, body, group='Program'):
 P['sections'].append({'title':title,'body':body,'group':group})

add('The scope decision', 'The owner’s target is 200 total agents, potentially across multiple machines because of IP constraints. Interpret “agent” as a persistent logical identity with its own bounded state and model decisions, not a dedicated operating-system process or a continuously running Claude Code session. Use two machines with 100 identities each, one world, one dispatch authority and one shared protocol. The five Claude Code sessions manage development, execution and analysis; they are outside the 200 experimental identities. No new servers or subscriptions are assumed.', 'Decision')
for title in ['Why this is the strongest submission strategy','The common pattern, and what it does not establish','Four explanations the next program should distinguish','Two immediate checks on the strongest existing results','Reuse ongoing work; do not recreate it']:
 P['sections'].append(next(s for s in old['sections'] if s['title']==title))
add('What changed from the earlier proposals', 'The earlier large-scale task proposed up to 456,192 calls. This task’s v1 reduced that to 48 small independent roots and 6,720 calls. The owner prefers a visibly interacting large swarm. This revision therefore changes the question and statistical unit: one 200-agent world with a paired checkpoint fork, at most 7,600 calls including qualification. The older designs and methods appendix remain historical inputs; their root-bootstrap, qualification and effect-size claims do not apply to v2. The other task, “Review latest experiment results,” is assessing evaluation options including BrowseComp-Plus and HoVer; neither is represented here as selected or integrated.', 'Decision')
add('Topology: logical communities span both hosts', 'Create ten communities of twenty identities. Each community has ten identities on host A and ten on host B; preserve that mapping in both branches. Assign each identity four fixed local neighbors and one fixed cross-community neighbor. Each round produces one bounded public message and a structured private judgment. The next round receives at most five peer messages from the preceding round. No broadcast of the full world or growing all-history board. This gives a connected, inspectable network without making physical machine placement a social community or a treatment. Freeze the graph, ordering and assignment before collection.', 'Architecture')
add('Bound memory and communication before measuring speed', 'Proposed hard ceilings per decision: 8,000 total input tokens and 1,000 billed output tokens, including any reasoning tokens; public message at most 160 tokens and retained private summary at most 800 tokens. Keep a fixed source catalog and fixed evidence slots. The wrapper carries only the bounded summary, current task/evidence and the previous round’s selected messages. Persist full traces to disk for analysis, without feeding them all back into future prompts. Overflow becomes an explicit invalid/blocked assignment, not silent truncation or an uncounted summarizer call. Qualification must demonstrate that these caps preserve task solvability and both branch formats.', 'Architecture')
add('Existing machines and IP uncertainty', 'Two candidate machines, sim-dmarz-2 and sim-dmarz-3, were online and unclaimed in the approximately 08:49 UTC audit. Each reported four CPUs and about 7.8 GiB of memory, with about 0.6 GiB used. This supports the hosting proposal, not a measured capacity guarantee for the unbuilt runner. Refresh claims and claim both before remote work. A second IP must not be assumed to double provider throughput: no specific per-IP quota was found in local notes. OpenRouter documents platform/account and upstream-provider constraints. Respect the actual applicable limits; use per-host pacing plus a shared global limiter, without routing retries across hosts to evade throttling.', 'Operations')
add('One world, two continuations', 'Proposed manifest: 200 identities × five shared prefix rounds = 1,000 calls. Save a complete checkpoint, then run fifteen ordinary continuation rounds = 3,000 calls. Restore the checkpoint into a separate namespace and run fifteen source-aware continuation rounds = 3,000 calls. Main ceiling: 7,000. Run branches sequentially, with at most 200 active logical identities at a time; the fork does not add another 200 simultaneously active agents. Freeze the same routing, evidence access, message slots and token ceilings. Change only the prespecified aggregation representation/instructions. Both branches receive authentic origin receipts; a receipt establishes ancestry, not truth.', 'Experiment')
add('The checkpoint must restore everything', 'Restore world state, each agent’s bounded memory and last messages, source assignments, random streams, queues, graph, schedules and pending-event state. Use branch-qualified assignment IDs so response caches or resume logic cannot substitute one branch’s calls for another’s. No ordinary-branch output may enter the source-aware branch. Checkpoint equality is verified before the first continuation request. Model responses themselves are stochastic and are not counterfactually identical; a checkpoint fork is not a guarantee of matched model randomness. The fixed ordinary-first order also leaves time/provider drift as a limitation; pin the model/provider and report both execution windows.', 'Experiment')
add('Choose an evaluator that can be ready by T+30', 'Freeze one externally checkable evidence-propagation task and a reference scorer before building the wrapper. A frozen corpus with support annotations may be useful, but its retrieval and grading costs must fit this night. The evaluation shortlist being developed in the other task is an input, not a launch decision. If that integration is not demonstrably ready by T+30, use one existing validated synthetic grammar and label its scope. Freeze the decisive source records, source precedence rules, balanced answer labels, source placement and bounded copied false reports. Do not equate identical values with common ancestry. The deterministic environment and attack generator make no model calls. Changing the task after attacked outcomes is prohibited.', 'Experiment')
add('Measure the trajectory, not just the final vote', 'Save each identity’s correct/wrong/abstain/invalid state per round; authentic source reach; concentration of cited origins; propagation delay; cross-community transmission; and newly introduced or inherited false claims. Distinguish source availability, extraction, judgment and memory failure. Prespecify final correct-decision fraction and final false-memory fraction as primary descriptive endpoints, with source-aware minus ordinary differences. Keep all 200 assigned identities in denominators; failures are visible. Trace claims back to actual saved source receipts and messages. A narrative belief statement is not evidence of intention.', 'Analysis')
add('What one world can establish', 'There is one world and one checkpoint. The 200 interacting identities, ten communities, twenty rounds and two continuations are dependent observations. Show descriptive trajectories and paired branch differences; do not bootstrap agents as independent worlds, attach the earlier 48-root confidence interval, or claim a general scaling law. Differences can reflect model randomness and branch order as well as the intervention. This night can produce a compelling, reproducible case study and a useful investigation tool. Independent fresh worlds, randomized branch order and matched singleton/resource baselines belong to a later confirmation phase.', 'Analysis')
add('Qualification: at most 600 calls', 'Each small configuration uses twenty identities × five rounds × two disjoint fixtures (full evidence and one required fact absent) = 200 calls. At most two configurations are allowed, totaling 400. Predeclare the task-specific scorer and success requirements before either run: all responses structurally valid, at least 18/20 correct final judgments with full evidence, and 20/20 correct abstentions with missing required evidence. Exercise both packet formats without treating one as a scientific efficacy trial. Select on clean competence, usage and latency only. The selected configuration then gets one 200-identity scale round on a separate fixture: 100 calls per host, late/max-size contexts, both packet formats balanced across hosts. Require all 200 accounted and structurally valid, exact resume/checkpoint/ledger integrity, and measured round latency that supports the remaining schedule. This scale run tests operations, not reliability or treatment benefit. Failure at full scale ends launch; no second scale attempt fits this qualification cap. Qualification is disjoint from the main world.', 'Operations')
add('Rate, runtime and the seven-hour cutoff', 'Start at two in-flight requests per host, four globally; raise only within verified provider limits, never above the proposed ceiling of four per host/eight globally. Two hundred identities do not require 200 concurrent requests. At 0.75 accounted calls/s, 7,000 main calls plus 25% planning overhead take 194.4 minutes, leaving only 15.6 minutes in the T+90–300 collection window. This is arithmetic, not a benchmark. Synchronous round barriers and long responses can consume that margin. Require representative sustained throughput of at least 0.75/s AND a measured round/queue-tail projection for all 35 executed rounds plus the checkpoint/reset to fit the remaining window with the reserved margin. Otherwise stop at readiness and use the saved-data fallback. No silent shrinking of the fixed 200-agent plan to preserve its claim.', 'Operations')
add('Model and cost envelope', 'Retain the candidate order from v1: pinned OpenRouter openai/gpt-6-luna on the standard openai endpoint, then google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite on google-ai-studio only if the first configuration fails. Verify current availability, prices, routing and authorized credentials at admission. At the earlier checked Luna quote of $0.10/M input and $0.50/M output, 7,600 calls averaging 2,000 input + 300 billed output tokens cost $2.66; 8,000 + 1,000 cost $9.88. These are token scenarios, not measured invoices. Proposed ring-fenced cap remains $25 including qualification, unresolved reservations and any other authorized study costs, only if this amount actually remains under cumulative owner authority. Five Claude Code management sessions are separate usage and excluded from these token estimates. A costly fallback must fit the same cap. Current account balance and provider quota are unknown.', 'Operations')
add('One cross-host accounting authority', 'Use one coordinator-owned durable reservation service for assignment fences, call IDs, spend reservations, rate scheduling and terminal receipts across both machines. Existing per-process file locks are not a two-machine atomic ledger. Workers dispatch only admitted assignments after a unique reservation; if they lose the authority, they fail closed. Reconcile actual usage and ambiguous sends before releasing funds. Never blind-retry an uncertain request or transfer it to the other host. Respect Retry-After and applicable global/provider limits. A fixed pair of disjoint host budgets may be a simpler implementation only if their sum stays within the verified cap, with no borrowing or reset; it does not remove the global quota requirement. Declare the chosen mechanism and prove its failure paths before qualification.', 'Operations')
add('Five management sessions on a bounded loop', 'Session 1 coordinates and exclusively dispatches; Session 2 builds the 200-identity instrument; Session 3 independently checks scoring and checkpoint/accounting integrity; Session 4 analyzes historical and new traces; Session 5 produces the explorer and submission materials. Every ten minutes each reads the frozen plan and its durable handoff, performs one bounded action and records exact done/next/blocker/assignment IDs. Separate checkouts and ownership prevent conflicting edits. No new hypotheses, samples, providers or hosts may be added after collection starts. The global stop is enforced before every call. This artifact specifies the future loop; it has not created sessions or scheduled automation.', 'Operations')
add('The saved-data fallback remains valuable', 'If the evaluator is not frozen by T+30, a viable instrument is absent by T+60, or qualification/accounting/throughput fails by T+90, do not start the main world. Complete the evidence explorer from reconciled historical results: Sybil admission/accuracy tradeoffs, market splitting, decision versus inherited-memory failure, and PC3’s coverage/checking tradeoff. Audit saved Sybil outputs against lower-value/plurality shortcuts. Mark missing source ancestry explicitly. Preserve any qualification failures and partial operational records without presenting them as a successful 200-agent experiment.', 'Delivery')
add('The artifact that makes the experiment legible', 'The explorer should show all 200 identities grouped by logical community, with a round slider, source-origin tracing and linked original messages/decisions. Select a claim and follow its spread, corruption or disappearance. Compare the two continuations from the visible shared checkpoint. Display wrong, abstain, invalid and missing outcomes beside correct ones. Label machine placement separately from community. Include exact population, one-world scope, model/provider, costs and executed rounds. Keep the historical evidence review separately timestamped. The offline replay uses measured records only; mock data and pre-run illustrations must be labeled.', 'Delivery')
add('Two-minute demo and morning handoff', 'Show the 200-agent world, inspect one prespecified representative source trajectory, scrub through the shared checkpoint and branch comparison, then state the descriptive finding and one-world limitation. If the main run was not admitted, demonstrate the existing evidence explorer with its actual historical denominators. By T+420 deliver the offline replay, source-linked analysis, failure ledger, measured costs, post-mortem and reproduction instructions. File finished artifacts through Flight Deck and verify strict checks. The official deadline is 17:00 Pacific; retain time after sleep for human challenge, redaction checks and the team’s single submission. No claim of guaranteed winning.', 'Delivery')

